      "sourceTextSha256": "bbba0ab77b2b2d881abfd1b7e6bfe62143ccf92d4fe8a7270ab30b0d0304ff35",
      "text": "Over 12 days, this route takes you through four very different regions of Brazil. São Paulo introduces a metropolis with a historic centre, a Japanese neighbourhood, Avenida Paulista and Ibirapuera Park. In Manaus, the city gives way to the Amazon: boat trips, piranhas, a caboclo village, rainforest and the chance to see the famous Meeting of the Waters, where the Rio Negro meets the Solimões. Next come the classic views of Rio de Janeiro, before the journey ends at Iguazu Falls, seen from both the Brazilian and Argentine sides.",
